  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no archived ticket that reports this exact problem. That problem is Burn detecting and planning each per-user related bundle twice (wixtoolset/issues#7675). The first uninstall removes the cache. The second then fails with 0x80070003 and is treated as non-vital. The old entry is left in Installed Apps with a broken UninstallString. Three archived tickets are close but are different problems. PowerToys#42181 has the same trailing 0x80070003 'Failed to configure per-user related bundle' error, but it is about a corrupt install and was closed as a duplicate of #35949. It does not mention the duplicate detection. PowerToys#43774 and PowerToys#47250 show the same doubled 'Detected related bundle' lines for per-user bundles. Their actual failure is error 0x81f40001, a per-user and per-machine conflict. Please file this as a new installer issue. Link wixtoolset/issues#7675, include your Burn log excerpts, and ask for a Burn fix that deduplicates related bundles. Until that is fixed, you can't remove a stale entry from Installed Apps. The archive has no verified workaround for that.\"}",
